menu "NEO-M8N GPS Configuration"

config NEO_M8N_UART_NUM
    int "UART port"
    range 0 2
    default 2
    help
        UART peripheral the NEO-M8N is wired to. UART0 is normally taken by the
        serial monitor, so UART1 or UART2 is the usual choice.

config NEO_M8N_TX_GPIO
    int "TX GPIO (MCU -> module RX)"
    range -1 48
    default 17
    help
        Drives the module's RX pin. Needed only to configure the receiver over
        UBX; set to -1 for a receive-only wiring, which also requires turning
        off auto_config in neo_m8n_config_t.

config NEO_M8N_RX_GPIO
    int "RX GPIO (MCU <- module TX)"
    range 0 48
    default 16
    help
        Reads the module's TX pin. Always required.

config NEO_M8N_BAUD
    int "Initial baud rate"
    default 9600
    help
        The rate the module is speaking when the MCU starts, not the rate you
        want. A factory-fresh NEO-M8N uses 9600; change this only if the module
        has had a different rate saved into its flash.

        To run faster, leave this at 9600 and set target_baud in
        neo_m8n_config_t - the driver will switch both ends over.

endmenu
